# Supabase source, migrations and internal engineering records are Git-owned
# deployment inputs, never public website content.
#
# SECURITY FIX (2026-08-25, found during a Supabase RLS/authorization audit): the previous rules
# here used status code 404, which Cloudflare Pages' own redirects documentation does NOT list as
# a supported rewrite/redirect status (only 3xx redirects and a 200 rewrite are functional) --
# confirmed live in production, where a real file at this path was served in full (HTTP 200,
# genuine file content) despite this rule's presence, because Cloudflare Pages serves an existing
# static asset before evaluating an unsupported-status _redirects entry, not after. A 200 rewrite
# is the supported mechanism that actually masks the underlying file's content at its original URL
# -- verified working in production after this fix (see the repair ledger for the exact check).
#
# DEFENSE IN DEPTH (2026-08-25, same audit, follow-up pass): functions/_middleware.js is now the
# PRIMARY block for these paths (and a broader set of internal artifacts -- see its own header) --
# Cloudflare Pages Functions run ahead of both _redirects and static-asset serving on this project,
# and the Function normalizes case/percent-encoding itself rather than relying on _redirects' glob
# matching. These two rules are kept as a second, independent layer, not removed -- if the Function
# were ever accidentally removed or misconfigured, this layer still masks the two paths it covers.
/supabase/* /404.html 200
/GOVERNANCE/* /404.html 200
